IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gaq-common`
IMPORT `gaq-appointment`

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Queensland) -- worked cases for gaq-common.l4 (sch 4 capacity and paid
-- carer, s 11, sch 2) and gaq-appointment.l4 (ss 12-14, 21, 26, 28, 29, 31, 33, 155, 245).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (act-2000-008, in force from 2026-04-28), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario
-- life raised this Act; the facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Every "is satisfied" and "considers" of
-- the tribunal or a court is given as a fact.
--
-- A breached DEONTIC cannot be compared with EQUALS on the stable l4, so the s 21(1) rule is asserted through the
-- question that uses CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED, and one breach is #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`dmy` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

§ `sch 4 -- capacity`

-- A road-accident claimant with a brain injury who understands the claim but cannot weigh an offer free of a relative's
-- pressure lacks limb (b).
#ASSERT `Do I have capacity for the matter question` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you have capacity for the matter (sch 4, capacity)`
#ASSERT `Do I have capacity for the matter question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: you have impaired capacity for the matter (sch 4, impaired capacity), as you are not capable of every limb of capacity`
#ASSERT `Do I have capacity for the matter question` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: you have impaired capacity for the matter (sch 4, impaired capacity), as you are not capable of every limb of capacity`
#ASSERT `Do I have capacity for the matter question` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: you have impaired capacity for the matter (sch 4, impaired capacity), as you are not capable of every limb of capacity`
#ASSERT `Do I have capacity for the matter question` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you have impaired capacity for the matter (sch 4, impaired capacity), as you are not capable of every limb of capacity`

§ `s 11 -- the presumption`

#ASSERT `Must my capacity be presumed question` `the tribunal (QCAT) or the Supreme Court, deciding my capacity for the matter` FALSE EQUALS `you must be presumed to have capacity for the matter until the contrary is proven (s 11(1))`
-- Fork F5: a declaration in force does not displace s 11(1) for the tribunal or court deciding capacity again.
#ASSERT `Must my capacity be presumed question` `the tribunal (QCAT) or the Supreme Court, deciding my capacity for the matter` TRUE EQUALS `you must be presumed to have capacity for the matter until the contrary is proven (s 11(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my capacity be presumed question` `my guardian or administrator appointed for the matter` FALSE EQUALS `your guardian or administrator for the matter need not presume you have capacity for it (s 11(2))`
#ASSERT `Must my capacity be presumed question` `another person or body acting under the Act` TRUE EQUALS `they may rely on the declaration that you have impaired capacity for the matter and presume you do not have capacity for it (s 11(3))`
#ASSERT `Must my capacity be presumed question` `another person or body acting under the Act` FALSE EQUALS `s 11 gives this person no presumption either way`

§ `sch 2 -- the kind of matter`

-- A damages claim for a workplace injury.
#ASSERT `Which kind of matter is my claim question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `a financial matter: a legal matter relating to your financial or property matters, for an administrator (sch 2 ss 1(o), 18)`
-- A claim for an apprehended violence order or a discrimination complaint seeking only an apology.
#ASSERT `Which kind of matter is my claim question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `a personal matter: a legal matter not relating to your financial or property matters, for a guardian (sch 2 ss 2(i), 18)`
#ASSERT `Which kind of matter is my claim question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Which kind of matter is my claim question` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `sch 4 -- paid carer`

#ASSERT `Is my carer a paid carer question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A parent whose care is paid for only out of damages awarded for voluntary care: limb (b)(ii) excludes it.
#ASSERT `Is my carer a paid carer question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my carer a paid carer question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 12 -- appointment`

#ASSERT `Can an administrator be appointed for me question` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the tribunal may appoint one for the matter, on its own initiative or on your application, the public guardian's or an interested person's (s 12(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can an administrator be appointed for me question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the tribunal is not satisfied you have impaired capacity for the matter (s 12(1)(a)); capacity is presumed until the contrary is proven (s 11(1))`
#ASSERT `Can an administrator be appointed for me question` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the tribunal is not satisfied there is a need for a decision, or an unreasonable risk to your health, welfare or property (s 12(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can an administrator be appointed for me question` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the tribunal is not satisfied that without an appointment your needs will not be adequately met or your interests will not be adequately protected (s 12(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can an administrator be appointed for me question` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the tribunal is not satisfied you have impaired capacity for the matter (s 12(1)(a)); capacity is presumed until the contrary is proven (s 11(1))`

§ `s 13 -- advance appointment`

-- Born 15 March 2008: 17 1/2 on 15 September 2025, 18 on 15 March 2026, 19 on 15 March 2027, 23 on 15 March 2031.
#ASSERT `Can an advance appointment be made for me question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) (`dmy` 14 9 2025) TRUE EQUALS `no: you are not yet 17 1/2 (s 13(1))`
#ASSERT `Can an advance appointment be made for me question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) (`dmy` 15 9 2025) TRUE EQUALS `yes: you are at least 17 1/2 but not 18; the appointment would begin when you turn 18 and end when you turn 19, unless the tribunal orders a longer period (s 13(1), (3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can an advance appointment be made for me question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) (`dmy` 14 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `yes: you are at least 17 1/2 but not 18; the appointment would begin when you turn 18 and end when you turn 19, unless the tribunal orders a longer period (s 13(1), (3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can an advance appointment be made for me question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) (`dmy` 15 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `no: you are already 18; an ordinary appointment under s 12 is the route (s 13(1))`
#ASSERT `Can an advance appointment be made for me question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) (`dmy` 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `no: the tribunal is not satisfied of each reasonable likelihood s 13(1)(a)-(c) requires`
-- Born 31 August 2008: 210 months on is February 2026, which has 28 days, so 17 1/2 on 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Can an advance appointment be made for me question` (`dmy` 31 8 2008) (`dmy` 27 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS `no: you are not yet 17 1/2 (s 13(1))`
#ASSERT `Can an advance appointment be made for me question` (`dmy` 31 8 2008) (`dmy` 28 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS `yes: you are at least 17 1/2 but not 18; the appointment would begin when you turn 18 and end when you turn 19, unless the tribunal orders a longer period (s 13(1), (3), (4))`
#ASSERT `When does my advance appointment begin question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) EQUALS `dmy` 15 3 2026
-- Born 29 February 2008: 18 in the common year 2026, read as 28 February 2026 (F4).
#ASSERT `When does my advance appointment begin question` (`dmy` 29 2 2008) EQUALS `dmy` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `When does my advance appointment end question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`dmy` 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT `When does my advance appointment end question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`dmy` 15 3 2027)
-- Fork F6: the longer period of at most 5 years runs from the 18th birthday.
#ASSERT `When does my advance appointment end question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`dmy` 15 3 2031)
#ASSERT `When does my advance appointment end question` (`dmy` 15 3 2008) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `When does my advance appointment end question` (`dmy` 29 2 2008) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`dmy` 28 2 2031)

§ `s 14 -- who may be my administrator`

-- A sister, 30, who is not paid for care and not bankrupt, whom the tribunal considers appropriate.
#ASSERT `Can this person be my administrator question` `an individual` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the person is eligible and the tribunal considers them appropriate (s 14(1)(b), (c)); being your relative or a beneficiary of your estate does not of itself mean a conflict (s 15(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can this person be my administrator question` `an individual` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: an individual administrator must be at least 18 (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can this person be my administrator question` `an individual` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: your paid carer or health provider cannot be your administrator (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can this person be my administrator question` `an individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a bankrupt, or a person taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor, cannot be your administrator (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can this person be my administrator question` `an individual` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the tribunal does not consider the person appropriate, having regard to the s 15(1) considerations (s 14(1)(c))`
-- The individual limbs do not apply to the public trustee or a trustee company.
#ASSERT `Can this person be my administrator question` `the public trustee` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the person is eligible and the tribunal considers them appropriate (s 14(1)(b), (c)); being your relative or a beneficiary of your estate does not of itself mean a conflict (s 15(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can this person be my administrator question` `a trustee company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the tribunal does not consider the person appropriate, having regard to the s 15(1) considerations (s 14(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can this person be my administrator question` `another kind of body` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: only an individual, the public trustee or a trustee company may be an administrator (s 14(1)(b))`

§ `s 245 -- the court that approves my settlement`

-- A District Court personal injury claim settled for an injured person with a brain injury.
#ASSERT `Can the court appoint my administrator question` `the District Court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court may itself appoint an administrator (or guardian) for you, with all the tribunal's chapter 3 powers, and must send the tribunal a copy of its order (s 245(2)-(4))`
#ASSERT `Can the court appoint my administrator question` `the Supreme Court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court may itself appoint an administrator (or guardian) for you, with all the tribunal's chapter 3 powers, and must send the tribunal a copy of its order (s 245(2)-(4))`
#ASSERT `Can the court appoint my administrator question` `another court (for example the Magistrates Court)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 245 applies only in the Supreme Court or the District Court (s 245(7)); the tribunal may still be asked under s 12`
#ASSERT `Can the court appoint my administrator question` `the Supreme Court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 245 applies only when the court sanctions a settlement (including a compromise or taking money paid into court) or orders money paid to you (s 245(1)(a)); the tribunal may still be asked under s 12`
#ASSERT `Can the court appoint my administrator question` `the District Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 245 applies only if the court considers you have impaired capacity for a matter (s 245(1)(b))`

§ `s 21(1) -- the registrar of titles`

-- Appointed 30 November 2026: 3 months on is February 2027 (28 days), so the last day is 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `Last day to advise the registrar of titles question` (`dmy` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `dmy` 28 2 2027
-- Appointed 30 November 2027: February 2028 has 29 days.
#ASSERT `Last day to advise the registrar of titles question` (`dmy` 30 11 2027) EQUALS `dmy` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `Last day to advise the registrar of titles question` (`dmy` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `dmy` 15 4 2027
#ASSERT `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time question` FALSE (`dmy` 30 11 2026) FALSE (`dmy` 1 1 2027) (`dmy` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `s 21(1) does not apply: the appointment does not involve an interest in land`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time question` TRUE (`dmy` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`dmy` 28 2 2027) (`dmy` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `yes: your administrator advised the registrar of titles within 3 months of the appointment (s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time question` TRUE (`dmy` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`dmy` 30 11 2026) (`dmy` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `yes: your administrator advised the registrar of titles within 3 months of the appointment (s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time question` TRUE (`dmy` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`dmy` 1 3 2027) (`dmy` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `no: your administrator advised the registrar of titles late; that is a ground for removal at review (s 31(5)(c))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time question` TRUE (`dmy` 30 11 2026) FALSE (`dmy` 1 1 2000) (`dmy` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `not yet due: the 3 months have not ended (s 21(1))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time question` TRUE (`dmy` 30 11 2026) FALSE (`dmy` 1 1 2000) (`dmy` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `overdue: the 3 months have ended and your administrator has not advised the registrar of titles; that is a ground for removal at review (s 31(5)(c))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time question` TRUE (`dmy` 30 11 2027) TRUE (`dmy` 29 2 2028) (`dmy` 1 6 2028) EQUALS `yes: your administrator advised the registrar of titles within 3 months of the appointment (s 21(1))`

-- 90 days allowed (30 November 2026 to 28 February 2027); nothing done by day 91.
#TRACE `s 21(1) -- the administrator advises the registrar of titles` 90 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 91)
-- expect: BREACH by the administrator, "s 21(1): the administrator did not advise the registrar of titles within 3 months ..."

§ `s 26 -- automatic revocation`

#ASSERT `Has my administrator's appointment ended question` `my administrator became my paid carer or health provider` EQUALS `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator's appointment ended question` `my administrator became the service provider of the residential service where I live` EQUALS `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator's appointment ended question` `my marriage to my administrator, in place when they were appointed, was dissolved` EQUALS `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator's appointment ended question` `my civil partnership with my administrator, in place when they were appointed, was terminated` EQUALS `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator's appointment ended question` `my administrator died` EQUALS `yes: the appointment has ended because your administrator died (s 26(1)(e))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator's appointment ended question` `my administrator became bankrupt or insolvent` EQUALS `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(2)(a), (3))`
#ASSERT `Has my administrator's appointment ended question` `something else` EQUALS `no: s 26 does not end the appointment on this event; it ends otherwise only on withdrawal with the tribunal's leave (s 27) or at a review (s 31)`

§ `s 28 -- periodic review`

#ASSERT `By when must my appointment be reviewed question` FALSE (`dmy` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`dmy` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`dmy` 1 7 2031)
#ASSERT `By when must my appointment be reviewed question` FALSE (`dmy` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`dmy` 1 7 2028) EQUALS JUST (`dmy` 1 7 2028)
-- An order day later than 5 years is capped at the 5 years ("at least every 5 years").
#ASSERT `By when must my appointment be reviewed question` FALSE (`dmy` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`dmy` 1 1 2032) EQUALS JUST (`dmy` 1 7 2031)
#ASSERT `By when must my appointment be reviewed question` FALSE (`dmy` 29 2 2028) FALSE (`dmy` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`dmy` 28 2 2033)
#ASSERT `By when must my appointment be reviewed question` TRUE (`dmy` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`dmy` 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 29 -- asking for a review`

#ASSERT `Can I ask for a review of the appointment question` `the adult (me)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a review of the appointment question` `an interested person for the adult` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a review of the appointment question` `the public trustee or a trustee company` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a review of the appointment question` `someone else` EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 31 -- the review outcome`

#ASSERT `What can the review do question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the appointment must be revoked: the tribunal is not satisfied it would appoint on a new application (s 31(2))`
#ASSERT `What can the review do question` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the tribunal may continue or change the order, and may remove your administrator (s 31(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `What can the review do question` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the tribunal may continue or change the order, and may remove your administrator (s 31(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `What can the review do question` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the tribunal may continue or change the order, but may not remove your administrator: it does not consider them no longer competent or another person more appropriate (s 31(3), (4))`

§ `s 155 -- suspension`

#ASSERT `Latest end of my administrator's suspension question` (`dmy` 15 11 2026) EQUALS `dmy` 15 2 2027
#ASSERT `Latest end of my administrator's suspension question` (`dmy` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `dmy` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `Latest end of my administrator's suspension question` (`dmy` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `dmy` 1 3 2027

§ `s 33(2) -- the administrator and my claim`

#ASSERT `Can my administrator settle my claim question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: your administrator may bring, run and settle the claim as you could if you had capacity (s 33(2), sch 2 s 18(d))`
#ASSERT `Can my administrator settle my claim question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: your administrator's appointment does not cover the claim, or the tribunal has ordered otherwise (s 33(2))`
#ASSERT `Can my administrator settle my claim question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the claim is not a financial matter, so it is for a guardian, not your administrator (s 33(2), sch 2 s 2(i))`
